From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@aeltra.eu>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 19:38:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] libfetch: retry the read after SSL_ERROR_WANT_READ/WANT_WRITE

On a non-blocking socket SSL_read() can return -1 with WANT_READ or
WANT_WRITE to ask the caller to wait for the socket and try again.
fetch_read() records the direction to wait for in conn->buf_events, but
then breaks out of the switch with rlen still -1, falls through to

	if (errno != EINTR || !fetchRestartCalls)
		return (-1);

and returns an error.  errno at that point is whatever OpenSSL last left
behind, so the retry the function has just set up never happens and a
perfectly recoverable condition is reported as a failed read.

Continue the loop instead, so the poll() at the top waits for the
recorded event before retrying.

For that to be safe the poll has to run whenever there is an event to
wait for, not only when a timeout is configured -- otherwise the retry
would spin.  Wait indefinitely when fetchTimeout is unset, which is what
a blocking socket does anyway.  The visible change for callers that set
no timeout is one extra poll() before each read; the semantics are
unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@aeltra.eu>
---
 libfetch/common.c | 20 ++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libfetch/common.c b/libfetch/common.c
index b2db699..66a7393 100644
--- a/libfetch/common.c
+++ b/libfetch/common.c
@@ -600,13 +600,17 @@ fetch_read(conn_t *conn, char *buf, size_t len)
 	pfd.fd = conn->sd;
 	for (;;) {
 		pfd.events = conn->buf_events;
-		if (fetchTimeout && pfd.events) {
+		if (pfd.events) {
 			do {
-				timeout_cur = compute_timeout(&timeout_end);
-				if (timeout_cur < 0) {
-					errno = ETIMEDOUT;
-					fetch_syserr();
-					return (-1);
+				if (fetchTimeout) {
+					timeout_cur = compute_timeout(&timeout_end);
+					if (timeout_cur < 0) {
+						errno = ETIMEDOUT;
+						fetch_syserr();
+						return (-1);
+					}
+				} else {
+					timeout_cur = -1;
 				}
 				errno = 0;
 				r = poll(&pfd, 1, timeout_cur);
@@ -625,10 +629,10 @@ fetch_read(conn_t *conn, char *buf, size_t len)
 				switch (SSL_get_error(conn->ssl, rlen)) {
 				case SSL_ERROR_WANT_READ:
 					conn->buf_events = POLLIN;
-					break;
+					continue;
 				case SSL_ERROR_WANT_WRITE:
 					conn->buf_events = POLLOUT;
-					break;
+					continue;
 				default:
 					errno = EIO;
 					fetch_syserr();
